      "id": "shattered-gate",
      "kind": "threshold",
      "title": "The Shattered Gate",
      "prose": "The bronze gates of Vharesk hang open, warped like melted wax. Beyond them, the capital's heart pulses with a sick violet light, visible even at midday. The air tastes of copper and rot. Somewhere below, the Bloomheart is waking, and you have perhaps three hours before it finishes.",
      "readAloud": "The city does not welcome you. It merely fails to stop you.",
